{
  "description": "CR 613.7f turning face up restamps the permanent after a removal that had wiped its grant",
  "note": "Repeat Offender is the suspect, suspecting itself with its own {2}{B}: a real road to CR 701.60c's designation, where the Haskell test wrote it onto an Ainok Tracker. Suspected is no ability of the card (CR 701.60b), so CR 708.2 leaves it alone and its grant carries the permanent's own timestamp into layer 6 (CR 613.7a); that grant is the one effect on the board whose order against Turn to Frog's removal a turning-over can move. Turn to Frog is a spell, so CR 613.7b stamps it as it resolves. bob's other Goblin Piker, never suspected, is the anti-vacuity leg: it blocks. Ixidron turns it face down first; Turn to Frog then resolves later than that stamp, so the removal is the younger effect and menace is gone (CR 613.1f). Break Open turns it face up by an effect, and CR 613.7f stamps it again past the removal: menace is back and it can't block, while the other Piker blocks.",
